Mudd is given away free of charge, and so must be everything made from it.


Definitions

"The Software" means Mudd: its source code, its builds, and its documentation.

A "Derived Work" is anything that includes the Software or any part of it, changed or not,
including a translation into another programming language or a port to another platform.


1. What you may do

Anyone who receives a copy of the Software may, free of charge:

  - use it for any purpose, including at work and in a business;
  - copy it;
  - change it; and
  - share it and Derived Works with others,

as long as they follow the conditions below.

Using the Software, for example to run your own company's sales prospecting, is not selling it
and needs no further permission.


2. No charge

You may not sell the Software or any Derived Work, or ask for or accept payment in exchange for
it. That includes:

  - charging to download, install, unlock or keep using it;
  - selling licenses or subscriptions to it;
  - putting it, or any feature of it, behind a paywall; and
  - offering it, or a service built on it, as a paid hosted service.

Voluntary donations are allowed, provided that donating unlocks nothing.


3. Share alike

If you share a Derived Work with anyone, you must:

  a. share it free of charge, under this license, with no added terms that take away any of the
     permissions this license grants;
  b. make its complete source code available, free of charge, to everyone you share it with; and
  c. say that it was changed from Mudd, and mark what you changed.


4. Notices

Every copy of the Software or a Derived Work, in whole or in part, must keep the copyright notice
above and a copy of this license.


5. No warranty

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT
NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND
